course: dictionary
lesson: 11632
title: Hard work over a long time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how hard something is. Arduous is one of them. It means very hard and tiring, needing a lot of effort for a long time. «The climb to the top of the mountain was arduous.» The climb was not just tricky. It was hard work that went on and on.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «After six hours of walking through mud and rain, the hikers were exhausted. It was an arduous journey.» The words six hours, mud, rain and exhausted tell you the journey was hard and tiring, so arduous must mean very hard. Test it: "It was a very hard, tiring journey." It fits.
explain: Arduous is not the same as difficult. A tricky puzzle can be difficult for a minute. An arduous task takes a long time and a lot of effort. «Training for the race was arduous: every morning for a year, she ran in the rain.» The word tells you about the time and the effort, not just the difficulty.
fact: Arduous means very hard and tiring.
fact: An arduous task needs a lot of effort for a long time.
fact: «An arduous journey» means a long, hard trip.
fact: Arduous is an adjective: arduous, more arduous, most arduous.
fact: Arduous is often used in stories, history and news about climbs, long journeys, work and training.
exercise: «The explorers faced an arduous trek across the desert.» What does arduous mean? | *Very hard and tiring | Cold and icy | Full of colourful flowers | Quick and easy
exercise: Which task is arduous? | *Digging a huge garden by hand over many weeks | A short game of catch | Sorting three buttons | Reading one page of a book
exercise: «The arduous work took all summer.» Which word means about the same as arduous? | quiet | *hard | sweet | happy
test: «Training for the marathon was arduous, with runs every day for months.» What does arduous suggest? | A sleepy afternoon | *Hard work over a long time | A quick, easy game | A sudden surprise
test: What is the difference between arduous and difficult? | Difficult means very old | They mean exactly the same, with no difference at all | Arduous means colourful | *Arduous adds the idea of long, tiring effort
exam: Which sentence uses arduous correctly? | The arduous sun was singing | The arduous puppy slept on the bed | The arduous sandwich was tasty | *The arduous climb took the whole day
